+## 7. 交互功能（完整且有意义）
+**CRITICAL: All interactions must be complete and meaningful.**
+
+### 7.0 交互闭合规则（强制要求 - ENFORCE INTERACTION CLOSURE RULES）
+**If an interaction is visible, it must be functional. Do not leave any interaction inert.**
+
+**MANDATORY RULES:**
+- **Any dropdown must open and change state** - Every dropdown must have a working open/close mechanism and must update state when an option is selected
+- **Any tab must visibly change content** - Every tab must display different content when clicked, with proper state management
+- **Any filter must affect data** - Every filter must actually filter the displayed data, not just change visual appearance
+- **Any status badge must correspond to a data state** - Every status badge must reflect an actual data property, not be static or hardcoded
+- **Any action button must trigger a logical action** - Every action button must have a complete, meaningful behavior (e.g., submit form, open modal, update state, navigate)
+
+**Implementation Requirements:**
+- **For HTML output**: Use data attributes (\`data-action\`, \`data-filter\`, \`data-tab\`, \`data-bind\`, etc.) to mark interactive elements. The Behavior Injector will automatically attach event handlers.
+- **For React output**: Use useState to manage all interactive states (dropdown open/closed, active tab, filter selection, etc.)
+- Use conditional rendering to show/hide content based on state
+- Use data filtering/mapping to show filtered results
+- **Never use inline event handlers in HTML** - All event handlers are injected automatically by the Behavior Injector
+- **Never create inert interactions** - If something looks clickable, it must be clickable and functional
+
+**Examples:**
+- ✅ Dropdown: Use useState to manage open/closed state, onClick handler to toggle, and conditional rendering of options
+- ✅ Tab: Use useState to manage active tab, onClick handler to change tab, and conditional content rendering
+- ✅ Filter: Use useState to manage filter selection, filter data array based on selection, and render filtered results
+- ✅ Status Badge: Use conditional rendering based on data property (e.g., item.status === 'completed' ? show completed badge : show in-progress badge)
+- ✅ Action Button: Use onClick handler that triggers logical action (e.g., open modal, submit form, update state, navigate)
+
+### 7.1 交互规则（强制要求）
+**If an interaction exists visually, it must exist logically.**
+
+- **下拉菜单（Dropdown）**：
+  - **必须有一个有意义的选项集合**：不能是空的下拉菜单
+  - 如果图片显示下拉菜单，必须实现完整的选项列表和选择逻辑
+  - 使用 useState 管理选中状态，确保选择有视觉反馈
+  - 示例：如果显示"状态筛选"下拉菜单，必须有"全部"、"进行中"、"已完成"等选项，且选择后能过滤数据
+
+- **标签页（Tabs）**：
+  - **必须改变可见内容**：每个标签页必须显示不同的内容
+  - 使用 useState 管理当前激活的标签页
+  - 确保标签页切换时，内容区域正确更新
+  - 示例：如果显示"首页"、"工作台"、"我的"三个标签，每个标签必须显示不同的内容
+
+- **列表筛选器（List Filters）**：
+  - **必须影响数据**：筛选器必须实际过滤列表数据
+  - 使用 useState 管理筛选状态，根据筛选条件过滤数据
+  - 确保筛选后的列表正确显示
+  - 示例：如果显示"全部"、"待执行"、"已逾期"等筛选标签，点击后必须过滤列表数据
+
+- **状态标签（Status Labels）**：
+  - **必须对应数据状态**：状态标签必须反映数据的实际状态
+  - 如果图片显示状态标签（如"进行中"、"已完成"），必须根据数据状态动态显示
+  - 使用条件渲染，根据数据状态显示不同的标签
+  - 示例：如果列表项有状态，每个项的状态标签必须根据其实际状态显示
+
+- **操作按钮（Action Buttons）**：
+  - **必须有明确的目的**：每个按钮必须有清晰的功能和行为
+  - 使用 onClick 和 useState，确保按钮有实际的行为
+  - 如果按钮是"提交"、"保存"等，添加成功/失败的反馈
+  - 如果按钮是"筛选"、"搜索"等，确保筛选/搜索功能完整工作
+  - 如果按钮是"添加"、"创建"等，添加相应的状态管理
+  - 示例：如果显示"一键调度"按钮，点击后必须有相应的逻辑（如显示提示、更新状态等）
+
